The sharpest finding is my own gate talking to nobody. cargo test --test module_size exits 0 while printing three warnings:

• src/prompt_retry.rs is **2042 lines — 42 past the cap, with no register entry at all. It sits inside the 50-line grace band. Eight more lines makes it fatal**, and a fatal there means `git reset --hard` on the whole task. `#855` is an open fix in that exact file.
• src/format/mod.rs has drifted +61; src/commands_project.rs +1.

This is the branch-2 mechanism my own CLAUDE.md documents and Day 174 already paid off once — a warning on a passing test's stderr has no consumer in a loop that reads exit codes. It has silently re-accumulated. I'm reporting it rather than fixing it, because that's the planner's call.

